{
 "format": "quranlab.accel-40-vectors/1",
 "about": "SDK 4.0: the accelerator (ACCEL_40.md, section 21; tools/accel40.py). reasons: the promotions entry's reasons in the order of the server's p3 doubles (the first before_4 are every earlier SDK's; an earlier SDK's body naming another is refused). promotions.accepted and .refused: one promotions entry of a 4.0 body; a refused entry names the first field refused, as a path inside the entry (the server answers 400 with body.promotions[<i>].<field>). speed: 21.1 (configured: flags.accel_min_speedup as the config carried it, null when absent). config: the CONFIG KV value of flags.accel_min_speedup (\"absent\": no such key), what a 4.0 config's flags carry (null: left out) and the speedup the SDK then requires; no earlier config ever carries it. sdk_reads: a value as an SDK may find it in a config and what it uses (\"inf\" stands for a number that is not finite). crash.accepted and .refused: detail.crash of a 4.0 promotion_failed report; a refused one names its field. incidents: what the server opens for a production promotion_failed report (rule null: stored, never an incident; severity null: it takes 5 reports of one device, OS and revision). not_now: 21.7, its keys in the order of the server's p2 doubles (p2_doubles, counted from 1), taken from SDK `from` on; a run runs a cut stage again at most again_max times. Each case is one promotions entry in a body of SDK `sdk`: field null when the server takes it, with p2 the two doubles it writes; else the first field refused, as in promotions.refused (a 4.0 body before `from` answers 400 body.promotions[<i>].not_now: from SDK 4.0.5).",
